{  
   "requirements_analysis":{  
      "requirement_79":{  
         "description":"The system must protect against excessive torque sensing that could lead to mechanical or structural damage.",
         "analysis":"This requirement emphasizes the need for a mechanism within the system to detect and mitigate situations where torque levels exceed safe operational limits. Excessive torque can cause significant stress on mechanical components, potentially leading to failure or damage. The system should include sensors capable of accurately measuring torque in real-time and algorithms that define what constitutes 'excessive' based on the specific application's parameters. Upon detecting excessive torque, the system must initiate appropriate countermeasures, such as reducing power output, engaging safety locks, or alerting operators, to prevent damage.",
         "implementation_considerations":[  
            "Integration of high-precision torque sensors capable of real-time monitoring.",
            "Development of a dynamic threshold algorithm that adjusts 'excessive' levels based on operational context and historical data.",
            "Implementation of an automated response system for immediate action upon detection of excessive torque."
         ]
      },
      "requirement_38":{  
         "description":"Safety systems must continuously monitor yaw rate to identify potential loss of control or rollover risks.",
         "analysis":"This requirement focuses on the continuous monitoring of the vehicle's yaw rate, which is a critical parameter for assessing stability and control. A sudden change in yaw rate can indicate a loss of traction or an impending rollover situation, especially in high-speed maneuvers or adverse conditions. The system must include sensors to accurately measure yaw rate and algorithms capable of analyzing this data in real-time to detect anomalies indicative of potential safety risks. Upon identifying such risks, the system should alert the driver and/or take corrective actions automatically, such as adjusting braking force on individual wheels (Electronic Stability Control) or reducing engine power.",
